# Frontend ↔ Backend Integration for VisionSnare

## Goal

Replace the **fully mocked** detection pipeline in the React frontend with a **real** connection to the VisionSnare PyTorch model. The user uploads a video → it gets preprocessed (optical flow, MTCNN alignment) → fed into the CNN-LSTM model → frontend displays real/fake verdict with confidence score.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **The Pricing page** is currently a cosmetic placeholder — buttons don't do anything. Should we leave it as-is (since it's an FYP demo), remove it entirely, or do you want it functional?

> [!WARNING]  
> **Frontend text discrepancies detected** — the "How It Works" and "About" pages mention **"16-frame Sequences"** and **"NPR 2×2, 3×3, 4×4"** multi-scale grids. However, the actual model code uses:
> - **12-frame sequences** (`SEQUENCE_LENGTH = 12`)
> - **Only 2×2 NPR** ([SpatialNPR](file:///d:/Fyp_Project/GAN_DeepfakeVideos_Detection_Model/models/npr.py#5-49) in [npr.py](file:///d:/Fyp_Project/GAN_DeepfakeVideos_Detection_Model/models/npr.py) uses 2×2 patches only)
>
> I will fix these text references to match reality. If you intentionally want to keep the multi-scale language for presentation purposes, let me know.

> [!NOTE]
> The backend API will run **on the same machine** as the frontend dev server. No cloud deployment is assumed. The model checkpoint [model_best.pth](file:///d:/Fyp_Project/GAN_DeepfakeVideos_Detection_Model/checkpoints/model_best.pth) (44 MB) already exists at [checkpoints/model_best.pth](file:///d:/Fyp_Project/GAN_DeepfakeVideos_Detection_Model/checkpoints/model_best.pth).

